<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint Thomas Christians</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nasrani</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Saint Thomas Christians are the ancient Christian community of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerala">Kerala</a>, who trace their origin to the apostle Thomas and long used the East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syriac">Syriac</a> liturgy, which is why they are often called Syrian Christians. Their churches held privileges from local rulers, recorded in the Tharisapalli <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> plates of 849 for the church at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kollam">Kollam</a>, and they were prominent in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">pepper</a> trade.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saint-thomas-christians.jpg" alt="Saint Thomas Christians" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jogytmathew · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nasrani_cross.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
